    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0455" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/240</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-10">10 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >March</hi>, 1915</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am anxious to know
                    whether our note to Japan about the “requests” she made of China has gone
                    forward or not. The twelfth (Thursday of this week) is the day named in the
                    despatches on which China must yield or ———? It would be well to have our note
                    in Japan’s hands by that date.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
